{
	title: 'Shipped extras: block-format EDIT and model-scoped EDIT quirks',
	spec: "extras/ holds tracked, ready-made plugins, off until selected like themes/: } from '../extras/<name>.ts'). Shipped changes take effect on host restart. ./test runs extras tests. extras/multiedit.ts replaces core EDIT and WRITE with one atomic block-format EDIT (!!OLD/!!NEW/!!END; line ranges, same-point inserts, text replaces after line operations, create, write; advisory @version; trailing actions run after a successful write), rewrites the # EDIT prompt section and drops # WRITE. Its parser is strict. extras/edit-quirks.ts wraps actions.resolve: a strict EDIT failure from a listed model (CallContext.model, a glob list per quirk) is retried after text rewrites, one per quirk, and each firing goes to state/diag.log with quirk, model and session; any other model, or none, gets the strict error unchanged. Quirks, seen from anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 in benchmarks (2026-10): $ command lines after the last block run as BASH; <invoke> call markup after the last block runs the actions it holds (also claude-opus-5-5); a lone stray word or doubled !!END after the last block is dropped; a bare action name or a trailing EDIT with no operations is dropped; an empty !!OLD/!!NEW replace is dropped; path@ with no version means path. Delete a quirk once its log shows no use. from \\'..\\/extras\\/<name>.ts\\')/a private plugins\\/<name>.ts wraps one in an inline export default (plugin) => { return extra(plugin) }, so \\/plugins disable and enable can toggle it}",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Replay of 376 block-format EDIT calls from sessions and benchmarks (2026-10-11): with a Sonnet context, multiedit+edit-quirks resolves all 376 exactly as the former lenient multiedit did (82 errors either way); with a GPT context, all 376 match strict multiedit alone (102 errors). Quirk firings are found from strict error text (the faulting line is located outside blocks by content), so they need no hooks inside multiedit. The former private native-multiedit tests were obsolete (they failed against the plugin) and were dropped.',
		'Undocumented tolerance (one documented form per job; others accepted silently): !!OLD closed by !!END removes the text; a text replace with empty new that matches whole lines once also removes their newline. delete A-B stays the documented way to remove lines.'
	],
	needs: ['pf2', 'vd9', 'an']
}
